  "findings": [
    "Removing only the contrast reward gains rotated star and rabbit crops but loses aircraft: 14 to 15 crop proposals. Removing only the purity term keeps 14 and the same proposed IDs.",
    "Full reconstruction regresses from 12 to 11 checked outputs: rabbit gained; aircraft crop and candle feature lost. Star reaches 0.7495% observed-mask disagreement but loses a 9.4375 square mm classified border feature. Geometry passes; overall template checks do not.",
    "The new rabbit passes at 0.5675% disagreement. The ship, fish and several checker borders still show reconstruction deviations; changed crop coordinates alter both the target and optimization trajectory.",
    "The checker reference corner error stays near 1.3% of side length (baseline 1.311%, no-contrast 1.334%). Better body/corner fits do not guarantee better templates.",
    "The printed-heart checker continues to confuse decoration with underlying paper: roughly 23.5% error on the independent known paper samples. Sparse interior labels do not certify the bicycle motif.",
    "All 23 accepted outputs pass editable checks. The one editable conversion failure is the no-contrast bicycle, already rejected by engine, feature and image checks. The controller failure is preserved, not overwritten as a pass."
  ],
  "nextStep": "Test a deterministic fallback only when the original cropper fails its unchanged support gates. Preserve accepted baseline crops; evaluate actual fallback selection and end-to-end exports before claiming an improvement. No best-arm union is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "Twenty-two repeatedly inspected development photographs, not an untouched test set.",
    "Derived masks are estimated artwork; low error is not original-template accuracy.",
    "Six approximate corner references and partial interior paper labels leave most photos unscored against independent source labels.",
    "Timed solves are not fully deterministic; changed crop targets also differ, so aggregate disagreement is not a fixed-target causal quality metric.",
    "No model or locator objective change is integrated into the application."
  ],
